Reference being entered (a *-led hole)
description: the pointer_entry state - typing is primary, the completion rides as an inline tail
- >
  The hole's text begins with `*` - the reference decision (keys.ts classifies it). THE
  TEMPLATE-CELLS RULE applies here too: the DECIDED row materializes as its temporary entry (a
  null value - an incomplete pointer has no valid IR - withheld from the wire), and the segment
  cells render as the value cell's template over the PICK cursor. The reference itself enters as
  SEGMENTS - the key-value gesture repeated: the cursor's `ref` carries the scope
  ladder, the committed segment cells and the active one (state.ts RefEntry; the half-typed
  reference lives in the cursor alone). `:` commits the active segment and opens
  the next; in the EMPTY FIRST cell it CLIMBS the scope ladder instead (`*` -> `*:` -> `*::` ->
  `*:::` - more colons, wider scope) and Backspace there steps it down. `[` in an empty non-first
  cell folds an INDEX onto the previous segment. Enter and Tab JOIN the segments and
  parse-or-refuse - non-pointers RING and the text stands, nothing is ever lost.
- >
  COMPLETION is an optional, advisory service over the same cells (complete.ts HintProvider -
  the pure editor answers from the in-memory document, the server host from the live tree over
  GET /api/query). **Typing is primary; the completer only helps.** Once the cell has text, the
  best candidate ARMS - the EXACT typed name first, then prefix matches, then substrings
  (rankHints; a fully-typed name can never lose to a lookalike) - and its untyped remainder
  rides IN THE CELL as the selected INLINE TAIL: any keystroke replaces it natively, `:` accepts
  it and opens the next segment, Enter/Tab accept it and finish. Arrows walk the dropdown and
  the tail follows the highlight. Escape closes the DROPDOWN and only the dropdown (the edit
  survives; typing reopens it); Delete discards the tail (the next typed character re-arms).
  An empty cell arms nothing. Hints ADVISE and never validate or gate typing - the grammar
  works identically with no provider at all.
- >
  The server mount also claims the shared TOC FILTER SESSION for the edit's lifetime
  (yed-toc-pick.ts, host-side - the pure editor stays TOC-blind): the typed query prunes the TOC
  and a TOC row click INSERTS the spelled path into the cells - the same advisory law as hints.
  A pointer has no SELF-VALUE form (the parser refuses a top-level pointer), so the omni
  diversion never applies: a BARE pointer lands as the KEYLESS member it is (`*x` is `- *x` -
  the chapter pointer-array case); only the `k:` enter-descend's EMPTY container takes it
  wholesale (`k: *x`).
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`alphanumeric`', 'native text in the active segment cell; the armed tail is replaced (it rides selected), then re-arms for the new prefix', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`colon`', 'the empty first cell, ladder below world - the SCOPE CLIMBS', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`colon`', 'otherwise - the ARMED SUGGESTION (if any) is accepted, the segment COMMITS, the next cell opens (a mid-text colon with no tail splits at the caret)', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`open_bracket`', 'an empty non-first cell - an INDEX folds onto the previous segment', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`up_arrow` / `down_arrow`', 'the dropdown is up - the highlight walks the list and the INLINE TAIL follows it; with no dropdown the caret walk leaves the cell', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`left_arrow` / `right_arrow`', 'at a cell edge - the walk crosses SEGMENT cells first, then leaves the reference', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`escape`', 'the dropdown is up - it CLOSES (and only it: the event never reaches the page''s lock-on-Escape); typing reopens it. With no dropdown the page''s own Escape law applies', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`delete`', 'an inline tail is up - the TAIL goes, the dropdown stays; the next typed character re-arms. With no tail, the grammar''s Delete (cells merge forward)', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`hint_pick`', 'a dropdown row click REPLACES the active cell''s text; the edit continues', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`toc_click`', 'the server mount only (yed-toc-pick.ts): the picked path SPELLS into the cells in the typed scope (pointer-spell, relative to the holder) - inserted like a hint, the caret on the last cell; typing meanwhile FILTERS the TOC through the shared session', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`enter` / `tab`', 'the armed suggestion (if any) is ACCEPTED, the joined segments parse as a pointer - it commits as the entry''s ref VALUE (dangling allowed; hints are never validators): SPACED canonical raw in the IR, COMPACT on the wire (yed-sync payloadOf). A reference holds no children, so the next SIBLING hole opens - the one exception to the level rule. Tab NEVER cycles the list; Shift-Tab keeps the level gesture', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`enter` / `tab`', 'not a pointer the wire can carry - the ring, the segments stand', '[error_flash](*::server:yamlover-editor:error_flash)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'a tail was up - the deletion also suppresses the tail (a deletion never fights a reappearing suggestion)', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'at the head of a non-first segment - the cells MERGE at the junction (the reference unwinds in reverse, segment by segment)', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the first cell''s head, ladder above bare - the SCOPE DESCENDS', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the emptied floor (one empty cell, bare scope) - the `*` decision undoes, the plain hole returns', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'otherwise', '`pointer_entry` (stays)']
